/-
# `kleinPt_corner`: the affine image of a cube corner

`Work.Cusp.cubeXToKlein a` is the affine map `x ↦ A x + b` from the UHS cube coordinates of the
cube `a : Fin 48` of the cusp development to the Klein model of `M̄` (see `Work.RTOwed.cuspDev`),
and `Work.Cusp.cubeCorner a` is the lower corner of that cube.  The identity proved here is the
elementary geometric fact behind the fibre-loop computation (`NOTES_SESSION3.md`, (G2)):

  the point `kleinPt a (cubeCorner a)` of the truncation facet is the point of the edge `[p_v,p_w]`
  of the truncated 24-cell which is cut off by the truncation `δ_K = 1/5`, namely
  `(3/5) p_v + (2/5) p_w` with `v = cubeIdeV a` (the ideal vertex of the cube) and `w = cubeWa a`.

The proof is a finite verification on the 48 cubes.  The tables are generated data and are stored
as 48-element literals, so unfolding them inside `simp`/`norm_num` in every one of the 192 goals is
expensive.  Instead this file carries, for each cube `a`, short `rfl` certificates that give the
value of every expression occurring in the goal as a literal (sliced verbatim from the definition
bodies, hence definitional equalities), and the main proof is then a `fin_cases` run over
`a : Fin 48` and `i : Fin 4` followed by `simp only` with those certificates and `norm_num`.

This file is generated by `_gen_kleinPt_corner.py`; do not edit by hand.
-/
